s sessions. 🤝 Session Handoffs: Automatically carries decisions, progress and context into your next AI session. 🛡️ Trust Guard: Verifies every optimization and automatically rolls back if a regression is detected. ⚡ Works Everywhere: One installation automatically configures Warden for 35+ MCP-compatible AI coding agents, including Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Windsurf, Cline, Roo Code, Continue, VS Code Copilot, JetBrains, Gemini CLI, Amazon Q and many more. Everything runs entirely on your machine. Warden doesn't require a cloud service, proxy your prompts, collect telemetry or send your code anywhere. Your repositories, tool outputs, memories and audit trail remain local, and the project is source-available, so anyone can inspect how it works. I'm proud of what I've built, but we also know the best developer tools are shaped by real developers using them on real projects, and as such, I'd love your help putting Warden through its paces. Install it, use it on real projects, and let us know how it performs. If you find a bug, open a GitHub issue. If you have an idea, request a feature. And if you'd like to contribute, pull requests are always welcome. If you find Warden useful, I'd also really appreciate⭐ giving the project a GitHub star and📢 please share it 🌍 Website: https://lnkd.in/dgQiDr-J ⭐ GitHub: https://lnkd.in/dXg_y-Kd Thanks for taking the time to check it out. I can't wait to hear your feedback, ideas and contributions—and see where the community helps take Warden next. cc Adii Pienaar — if you find this interesting, I'd love to hear your thoughts. #AI #MCP #ClaudeCode #Cursor #AIEngineering #ContextEngineering #DeveloperTools #LLM #BuildInPublic--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDaniel Eftekhari – Alchemist Media Labs | LinkedIn (https://de.linkedin.com/in/daniel-eftekhari-3a24a8227)\nciteturn26search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 months ago; \n🛠 Clear API contracts and predictable component structure. How 