Experimental AI shell assistant — ask questions, get shell commands, run an autonomous agent loop in your terminal.\n\nGitHub\n\n### ScrivaDB\n\nGo\n\nLightweight, embeddable, local-first database — single binary, NDJSON storage, gRPC/REST API, full CLI.\n\nGitHub\n\n### sp-treeview\n\nTypeScript\n\nMaterial-design tree view component for Angular, published on npm.\n\nGitHub\n\n### Pocket Money\n\nGo · React Native\n\nFamily-oriented chore tracking and pocket-money app — parents define and approve chores, kids log them and track their earnings and payouts.\n\n### Kept\n\nPython · React\n\nPrivate expense tracker\n\n## / About\n\nI've spent 10+ years in backend engineering at consumer scale — Gojek, Glovo, and now Affirm — the last several as a tech lead and then staff engineer. The part of the job I enjoy most is system design: mapping a messy problem into services, data models, and failure modes, and being able to argue the trade-offs at both the whiteboard level and the code level.\n\nI've worked across a wide spectrum of technologies rather than one stack — JVM services in Java, Kotlin and Clojure, systems tooling in Go, data pipelines over Kafka and RabbitMQ, and storage from Postgres to Redis to MongoDB.\n\nRecently I've been deep in AI-assisted development. After building spaiOS and spaiSH to explore the space, I landed on warden — and building it with fleets of AI agents (managed by warden itself) has been the fastest I've ever taken an idea from sketch to a mature, released tool.\n\n  1. Staff Software Engineer · Affirm\n\n2025 — present\n\nBackend, Barcelona.\n\n  2. Staff Software Engineer · Glovo\n\n2023 — 2025\n\nOwned the promotions platform architecture in the Growth domain — including its zero-downtime migration to a domain-driven design and a real-time pipeline ingesting millions of partner promotions daily.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAndy Warden - Three Plus Consulting | LinkedIn (https://uk.linkedin.com/in/andy-warden-67a08754)\nciteturn26search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; \n### 🧬Alexander Frey\n\n3mo\n\nAndy Warden liked this\n\nWir sollten langsam einen festen Platz für Awards im Büro einrichten... 😄🏆Carlo Luisa Ein riesiges Dankeschön an Workday für den Medium Enterprise Accelerator DACH Award 2026! Und noch viel wichtiger: Glückwunsch an das gesamte HR Path Team. Solche Auszeichnungen entstehen nicht durch Zufall, sondern durch Leidenschaft, Zusammenhalt und jede Menge Einsatz. Basolut... Ich bin gespannt, welcher als Nächstes dazukommt. 😉\n\nHR Path\n\n### HR Path\n\n3mo\n\nAndy Warden liked this\n\nWir haben gewonnen! Auf der Workday DACH Partner Summit 2026 durften wir den Medium Enterprise Accelerator DACH Award entgegennehmen, ein tolles Highlight für unser Team. Die Auszeichnung ist für uns mehr als nur ein Award, sie spiegelt das Engagement, den Teamgeist und die starke Zusammenarbeit wider, die unser HR Path Team ausmacht. Herzlichen Glückwunsch an unser gesamtes Team und ein großes Dankeschön an Workday für diese besondere Anerkennung! #WDPS2026 #Workday #WorkdayPartner #DACH #Partnership #Teamwork\n\n  * Andy Warden liked this\n\nAndy Warden liked this\n\nCome join us!\n\nHR Path\n\n### HR Path\n\n3mo\n\nAndy Warden liked this\n\nHR Path highlights exciting new job openings across the UK & Ireland! 🎯 Discover opportunities where you can make an impact, support HR transformation and grow your career in a collaborative international environment: PeopleXD Payroll & Workforce Management Consultant - Ireland 👉 https://lnkd.in/eY9nJdz5 Workday Payroll Senior Consultant - Ireland 👉 https://lnkd.in/eA8-q7R3 Senior Workday Consultant - Absence & Time Tracking - United Kingdom 👉 https://lnkd.in/e-7gFduB Workday AMS Consultant - United Kingdom 👉 https://lnkd.in/epBKj5H8 HR Administrator - Maternity Cover - Southampton, United Kingdom 👉 https://lnkd.in/ecdu2etB 🚀 Joining the HR Path group means becoming part of a fast-growing international HR and Payroll consultancy, with the opportunity to develop your expertise, work with talented teams and help clients get the best from their HR technology and people operations. Discover all current opportunities at HR Path and find the role that could be your next step. 👉 https://lnkd.in/dwTz4VFN #HRPath #UKJobs #IrelandJobs #WorkdayJobs #PeopleXD #PayrollJobs #HRISJobs #HRTech #ConsultingJobs #Hiring\n\n  * Andy Warden liked this\n\nAndy Warden liked this\n\nWhat a whirlwind the last few days have been. I am finally back from Workday DevCon in Las Vegas, though the journey home tried its absolute best to keep me there. A 1 hour layover in Amsterdam spiralled into an 8.5 hour endurance test. Needless to say, my first 24 hours back involved a massive 12 hour sleep reset on Friday night (the screenshot speaks for itself, my sleep score clearly needs some serious work) and immediately bouncing back to see Take That the next day. Now that the jet lag is clearing, I have had some time to digest the news, blogs, and major announcements from the event. The general consensus matches what we felt on the ground: Workday is fundamentally rewriting the enterprise developer playbook for the agentic AI era. Here are my key developer takeaways and the biggest talking points coming out of the conference: The Pivot Away from Sana Build: Leading up to DevCon, the general expectation was that custom agent development would revolve around Sana Agent Builder (effectively a rebranded Flowise) and surface strictly through the main Sana chat. Instead, Sana was barely mentioned on the development side. Sana Build and Flowise are gone from the agent development process. The New Extend Wrapper: Custom Agents are now firmly contained within an Extend App Wrapper. If you have Extend Pro, you can build traditional Extend Apps, Agent Only apps, or embed agentic functionality into broader apps with Business Objects and Business Processes. The Developer Agent Game Changer: Workday is aiming to shift development timelines from weeks to minutes. I managed to get some hands on time test driving it, and it honestly feels like a massive leap forward. What is getting a lot of love in the dev community is the flexibility, as it plugs directly into the tools we already use like Cursor, Cline, and Claude Code utilising the open AgentSkills standard. Open Front Ends via MCP: Crucially, these agents are not locked into Workday UI. Through Agent Ready Tools using the Model Context Protocol, they can be exposed to whatever front end your organisation uses, whether that is Microsoft Copilot, Gemini, or Claude. Taming the Wild West with Agent Passport: The other massive piece of news everyone is talking about is Workday Agent Passport, launched with Cisco as a primary partner. It is a new security framework that allows teams to test, verify, and continuously monitor agents against standards like OWASP and NIST before they hit production. It essentially acts as a centralised kill switch and compliance check for enterprise AI. The industry is calling this a major before and after moment for Workday, moving away from closed ecosystems and giving developers true velocity and flexibility without compromising enterprise governance.\n\npublic_profile__reactions\n\n`` ``\n\n34 `` `` `` `` `` `` `` 2 Comments\n\n  * Andy Warden liked this\n\nAndy Warden liked this\n\nGordon Cathcart\n\n### Gordon Cathcart\n\n4mo\n\nAndy Warden liked this\n\nJust finished an amazing day at Workday DevCon. There's a huge amount to digest from today's sessions, demos, and conversations. Developer Agent feels like a genuine game changer. The highlight, though, has been catching up with familiar faces and making new connections with talented developers from across the community. Events like this are a great reminder of the innovation happening across the platform. Looking forward to tomorrow and everything still to come. #WorkdayDevCon #LasVegas\n\n-------------------------------------------------------